Package: zak
Title: Install Remote Package Archives with Dependencies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "pedrobtz@gmail.com")
Description: Installs R packages from configured repositories, local
    directories, archives, or Git sources after resolving and
    installing their required dependencies. Installation is delegated to R's
    own package installer, and dependency resolution reproduces the package
    selection that installer performs. Provides inspectable plans, data-frame
    views of package databases, source provenance, static project discovery,
    package-project initialization, isolated project libraries, explicit
    activation, and versioned JSON lockfiles.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zak
BugReports: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zak/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    digest (>= 0.6.0)
Suggests:
    jsonlite (>= 1.8.0),
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
